  "notes": "The one clamp (M-26): rewatched seconds within a session count as genuine watch time, but they are bounded the same way looping is, watched_ms <= content_duration_ms x (loop_count + 1) whenever the duration is known, and the bound applies to every heartbeat's running total as well as the play_end figure. A scrub-back rewatch with no loop wrap therefore never credits more than one pass: 30000 here, with watched_ms_reported keeping the 40000 the client counted. Before M-26 the heartbeats had already carried 40000 past the play_end-only clamp through GREATEST."
